      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Early settlers built sawmills on Muddy Creek’s waterfall, with Noah Town’s 1833 mill among the first.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Townville%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Sawn lumber was rafted east to Oil Creek, then to the Allegheny River, reaching Pittsburgh.",
